 r←Test_Misc_036(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;report
⍝ Exercise `IsAvailableElsewhere`, which decides which rows of Tatin's "later versions" report name
⍝ a package the very same version of which is hosted by a Registry other than the one it came from.
⍝ Those rows are reported, and they are what makes `ReInstallFromDependencies` offer its re-install.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

⍝ The columns are: installed, latest, original URL, flag, new URL
⍝ [1] A later version: that is an update, not this
 report←1 5⍴'aplteam-Foo-1.1.0' 'aplteam-Foo-1.2.0' 'https://tatin.dev/' 1 'https://tatin.dev/'
⍝ [2] Nothing later, and the same Registry: nothing to say at all
 report⍪←'aplteam-Goo-2.0.0' 'aplteam-Goo-2.0.0' 'https://tatin.dev/' 0 ''
⍝ [3] Same version, different Registry: the only row that qualifies
 report⍪←'aplteam-Moo-1.0.0' 'aplteam-Moo-1.0.0' 'http://localhost:444/' 1 'https://tatin.dev/'
⍝ [4] A marker rather than a package ID, although [;5] names a Registry
 report⍪←'aplteam-Zoo-1.2.0-beta-2' '<<< Not available any more >>>' 'http://localhost:444/' 1 'https://tatin.dev/'
⍝ [5] Server did not answer
 report⍪←'aplteam-Woo-1.0.0' '<<< No response >>>' 'https://tatin.dev/' 0 ''

 →T.PassesIf 0 0 1 0 0≡##.Cider.IsAvailableElsewhere report

⍝ No row may be both: the two decide what happens to a row between them
 →T.PassesIf 0=+/(##.Cider.IsUpdateCandidate report)∧##.Cider.IsAvailableElsewhere report

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
